Help Type: topic
Topic: config

Configuration

Purpose:
  Configuration is managed through local Wiki Graph URIs, not by editing files directly.
  `wikg://local/config` is a namespace; operate on a child section.

Sections:
  `wikg://local/config/llm`
    LLM provider, model, optional base URL, client name, and API key.

  `wikg://local/config/embeddings`
    Embedding provider for Dense search index vectors and Dense query vectors:
      - `provider`: `openai` or `openai-compatible`.
      - `model`: embedding model name.
      - `dimensions`: optional positive integer when the provider/model supports dimension control.

  `wikg://local/config/concurrent`
    Local concurrency settings:
      - `job`: simultaneous generation jobs. Default: 3.
      - `request`: concurrent LLM requests. Default: 6.

  `wikg://local/config/wikimedia`
    Optional remote Wikimedia resolver:
      - `endpoint`: optional service base URL; defaults to the current development or production gateway.
      - `token`: required Bearer API key. A configured token enables remote resolution; an empty section keeps direct local Wikimedia access.

  `wikg://local/config/wikispine`
    WikiSpine runtime provider for Knowledge Graph builds:
      - `provider`: `cli` or `fetch`.
      - `endpoint`: optional service base URL for `fetch`; defaults to the current development or production gateway.
      - `token`: required Bearer API key for `fetch`.
      - `cli` runs the local `wikispine` command from PATH.

Operations:
  Read a section:
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/llm
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/embeddings
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/concurrent
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikimedia
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikispine

  Replace a section with a JSON object:
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/llm set '{"provider":"openai","model":"gpt-4.1"}'
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/embeddings set '{"provider":"openai","model":"text-embedding-3-small"}'
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/concurrent set '{"job":3,"request":6}'
    Sensitive tokens cannot be supplied by `set`; configure remote Wikimedia and WikiSpine incrementally with `put`.

  Update one key:
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/llm put provider openai
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/llm put model gpt-4.1
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/embeddings put provider openai
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/embeddings put model text-embedding-3-small
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/concurrent put job 3
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/concurrent put request 6
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikimedia put endpoint https://wikimedia.example.com
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikimedia put token --secret
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikispine put provider cli
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikispine put provider fetch
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikispine put token --secret

  Store the API key:
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/llm put apiKey --secret
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/embeddings put apiKey --secret

  Store a service token:
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikimedia put token --secret
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikispine put token --secret

Secret handling:
  - `apiKey` and `token` are read through an interactive hidden prompt.
  - `apiKey` and `token` are masked as `****` in command output.
  - `set <json>` and `set --json-input <json>` cannot set a real `apiKey`.
  - Those JSON inputs may include `"apiKey":"****"` to preserve an existing secret.
  - Omitting `apiKey` from those JSON inputs removes it from the section.

Minimum LLM-backed operation configuration:
  - `llm.provider`
  - `llm.model`
  - Provider credentials when required by the selected provider.

Minimum Dense embedding configuration:
  - `embeddings.provider`
  - `embeddings.model`
  - `embeddings.baseURL` when using `openai-compatible`
  - Provider credentials when required by the selected provider.

Dense search notes:
  - FTS artifact builds do not use this section.
  - Source and summary embedding artifact builds require this section.
  - Index cache sync does not call the embeddings provider; it uses vectors already stored in artifacts.
  - Query uses this section when the current index cache includes Dense vectors. If Dense query embedding fails, Hybrid query can still fall back to FTS.

One-run overrides:
  `--llm <json>` can provide an LLM object for one invocation.
  It accepts direct LLM objects and common OpenAI-compatible aliases such as `baseUrl`.
  A base URL implies `openai-compatible` when `provider` is omitted.
  Generation jobs may also receive `--llm <json>` at `{{ commandName }} wikg://local/job add`;
  that job-local LLM object is stored with the job and does not appear in `wikg://local/config/llm`.

Examples:
  {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/llm put provider openai
  {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/llm put model gpt-4.1
  {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/llm put apiKey --secret
  {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/llm test
  {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/embeddings put provider openai
  {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/embeddings put model text-embedding-3-small
  {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/embeddings put apiKey --secret
  {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/embeddings test
  {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikispine put provider fetch
  {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikispine put token --secret
  {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikispine test

Hosted provider environments:
  - `pnpm dev` uses `https://pdf-craft-api.oomol.dev`.
  - Built CLI artifacts use `https://api.pdfcraft.ai`.
  - An explicit provider endpoint overrides these defaults.

WikiSpine:
  Knowledge Graph builds require WikiSpine. If `wikispine` is missing,
  configure one provider and run the config test before starting Knowledge Graph work.
  - `fetch` uses the hosted service endpoint and requires network access plus a configured API key.
  - `cli` requires a `wikispine` executable on PATH and any local runtime/data it needs.
  - Test `cli` from the same shell that runs Wiki Graph; a different terminal or service environment may have a different PATH.
  - If `{{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikispine test` fails for `cli`, check PATH first or switch to `fetch`.
  - If the test fails for `fetch`, check network access and the API key, or switch to `cli` in environments with a prepared local runtime.
  - CLI help does not install the local WikiSpine runtime; use `fetch` unless the local runtime is already prepared.
  - Knowledge Graph jobs should not be started until this test succeeds.
  Runtime setup and recovery guide:
    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oomol-lab/wiki-graph/refs/heads/main/docs/wikispine-runtime.md

